  "adaptations": [
    "Finite selected OPSIN retained names and complete functional-class names; per-alias source token references remain in data.json.",
    "Independent explicit graphs index complete names; catalog order defines stable display order.",
    "One existing ChEBI retained (+)-lactic acid equivalence is selected; no other optical signs are inferred.",
    "Twenty amino-acid template identities, five usual nucleobase identities and ten Haworth sugar identities use the frozen asset SMILES (tautomer_smiles when specified).",
    "The separate frozen 7H adenine and guanine graphs retain plain OPSIN names, whose bundled tokens encode 7H; explicit 9H and 7H aliases never relax tautomer identity.",
    "Amino-acid D/L and sugar anomer/absolute configuration are matched exactly; unspecified and opposite configurations are not inferred.",
    "Template UI title case is normalized to conventional biochemical lowercase stems; L- prefixes and Greek sugar spelling remain explicit.",
    "Frozen cytosine uses 3H-cytosine. Frozen histidine has the opposite imidazole N-H tautomer to OPSIN histidine and uses 3-(1H-imidazol-5-yl)-L-alanine. Frozen arginine has the chain-imino guanidine tautomer and uses N(5)-(diaminomethylidene)-L-ornithine. These template graphs and aliases remain separate from plain OPSIN defaults.",
    "Three independent explicit graphs additionally index the strict bundled OPSIN defaults for L-histidine, L-arginine and cytosine. Each plain alias must reconstruct its own exact graph; no tautomer, stereochemistry or protonation relaxation is used."
  ],
